If you’re not using Tomcat and want to use WildFly (a Java EE / Jakarta EE application server) for production, your Spring Boot setup will be a bit different because:

🔧 By default:
Spring Boot apps are self-contained JARs that come with an embedded Tomcat (or optionally Jetty/Undertow).

But WildFly expects a WAR file and manages the server lifecycle separately.

✅ To deploy Spring Boot to WildFly:
Here’s how you can prepare your Spring Boot app:

1. Change packaging from JAR to WAR
In pom.xml:

xml
Copy
Edit
<packaging>war</packaging>
2. Exclude embedded Tomcat
xml
Copy
Edit
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
    <exclusions>
        <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-tomcat</artifactId>
        </exclusion>
    </exclusions>
</dependency>
And add:

xml
Copy
Edit
<dependency>
    <groupId>javax.servlet</groupId>
    <artifactId>javax.servlet-api</artifactId>
    <scope>provided</scope>
</dependency>
3. Extend SpringBootServletInitializer
In your main application class:

java
Copy
Edit
@SpringBootApplication
public class MyApp extends SpringBootServletInitializer {

    @Override
    protected SpringApplicationBuilder configure(SpringApplicationBuilder application) {
        return application.sources(MyApp.class);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(MyApp.class, args);
    }
}
4. Build WAR and deploy
Run:

bash
Copy
Edit
mvn clean install
Then deploy the generated target/*.war file to WildFly using its admin console or CLI.

Summary:
| Feature           | Embedded Tomcat         | WildFly Deployment          |
| ----------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Packaging         | JAR , WAR                    | WAR                         |
| Deployment style  | Standalone app          | Application server-managed  |
| Startup command   | `java -jar`             | Deploy to WildFly via admin |
| Servlet container | Embedded (Tomcat/Jetty) | Provided by WildFly         |


